{
  "dom_id": "step-q35843",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "In a particular country, there are two groups of people: those who are healthy and those who are sick. A study has shown that each quarter\n\n- $38%$ of the healthy people tend to get sick, and\n\n- $45%$ of the sick people tend to improve their health.\n\nWhich of the following tables describes how people's health status changes?",
  "worked_solution": "We are given the following situation for each semester: \n\n- $38%$ of the healthy people tend to get sick. This implies that $62%$ of them remain healthy.\n\n- $45%$ of the sick people tend to improve their health. This implies that $55%$ of them remain sick.\n\nWriting this information in tabular form, we obtain the following:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Healthy** | **Sick** |\n| To: | **Healthy** | $0.62$ | $0.45$ |\n| **Sick** | $0.38$ | $0.55$ |  |\n\nNote that we can write a corresponding stochastic matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0.62 & 0.45 \\\\ 0.38 & 0.55\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
